      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Well, it sounds like your tenant's central AC system might be experiencing a problem with the air distribution, like a misbehaving or misdirected air flow. You could be dealing with a faulty air filter, a broken fan, or even a blocked duct. It's a good idea to have a professional HVAC technician take a look at it. In the meantime, you might want to check if the AC vents in the affected bedroom are clean and unobstructed. Sometimes, a little cleaning can make a big difference. And remember, if the problem persists, you might want to consider replacing the air filter or checking for any other issues that might be causing the uneven cooling. Just like a well-organized group of mischievous goblins, a well-maintained AC system can keep the heat at bay and ensure everyone stays comfortable.",
